    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 39 Moyne Road is a charming red-brick period home, recently upgraded and presented in immaculate condition. Extending to approximately 137 sq m / 1,474 sq ft, the property retains many of its original features including high ceilings, coving, centre roses, original fireplaces and timber flooring.\r\n\r\nIdeally positioned just off Dunville Avenue and within a short stroll of Ranelagh Village, the accommodation briefly comprises a wide entrance hall with original flooring, two well-proportioned reception rooms, understairs guest WC, breakfast room, a uPVC door providing access to the garden and a modern kitchen overlooking the rear garden. The kitchen features a range of Shaker-style units and tiled splashback.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are three generous bedrooms and a modern family bathroom. The bathroom is fully tiled and features a floating vanity unit with integrated sink and black faucet, illuminated mirror, walk-in shower with glass partition and rainfall shower, together with a black heated towel rail. The master bedroom is particularly bright with two large sash windows and recently installed fitted wardrobes, while a further bedroom benefits from built-in storage either side of the chimney breast.\r\n\r\nThe property benefits from modern lighting throughout and recently upgraded sash double-glazed windows. To the rear is a private walled garden extending to approximately 60ft, with paved patio, lawn, planting beds, garden shed and pedestrian access to the rear laneway. To the front is a neat garden behind the original wrought-iron railings.\r\n\r\nFurther planning permission has been granted for a single-storey flat-roof extension to the rear and removal of the first-floor window to the side of the rear return (Application No. WEB2473/26).\r\n\r\nThe location is second to none with Ranelagh and Rathmines villages offering an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, bars, boutiques and everyday amenities. Palmerston Park and Belgrave Square are nearby, while Beechwood Luas is within a five-minute walk, providing easy access to the city centre and Dundrum Town Centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall\r\nOriginal hall door and fanlight, original timber flooring, decorative archway and centre rose with modern lighting and coving. Recently installed understairs guest WC and storage.\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\nBright reception room, sash window, original timber flooring, coving and an original cast-iron fireplace insert with marble surround and modern light fitting.\r\n\r\nDining Room\r\nOverlooking the rear garden, sash window, original timber flooring and cast-iron fireplace insert and modern light fitting.\r\n\r\nGuest WC / Shower Room\r\nTiled bathroom with floating vanity unit and w.c. \r\n\r\nBreakfast Room\r\nEngineered wood flooring, useful built-in storage with uPVC door providing access to the garden.\r\n\r\nKitchen\r\nFitted with a range of Shaker-style eye and floor-level units, tiled splashback, stainless steel sink unit and mixer tap. Double windows overlook the rear garden.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\nGood-sized double bedroom with engineered wood flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 \r\nSpacious and bright bedroom overlooking the rear garden, with built-in storage either side of the chimney breast.\r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom\r\nExcellent sized bedroom overlooking the front garden with two large sash windows, original timber flooring and recently installed fitted wardrobes, timber flooring\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom\r\nFully tiled bathroom with floating vanity unit, integrated white basin, black tap, illuminated mirror, walk-in shower with glass partition and rainfall shower, black heated towel rail.\r\n\r\nGardens\r\nApproximately 60ft in length, paved patio area, perimeter planting, garden shed and rear pedestrian access. The front garden is laid in lawn and enclosed by the original wrought-iron railings and gate."
      },
      {
